1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,580
What is diabetes? Diabetes is a serious condition where your blood sugar levels,

2
00:00:06,099 --> 00:00:11,679
also known as blood glucose levels, are too high. It's diagnosed from a blood test.

3
00:00:12,300 --> 00:00:17,579
There are two main types, type 1 and type 2, which is the most common.

4
00:00:18,399 --> 00:00:25,039
And lots of other types, like gestational diabetes, type 3c and modi.

5
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:32,679
The causes and symptoms depend on the type of diabetes you have. Diabetes happens

6
00:00:32,679 --> 00:00:39,420
because of a problem with a hormone called insulin. When you eat or drink, any carbohydrates

7
00:00:39,420 --> 00:00:47,539
you've had are turned into glucose, a type of sugar. Insulin acts like a key to unlock

8
00:00:47,539 --> 00:00:54,340
the cells to let the sugar in, to give you energy. If you have diabetes, this can't happen,

9
00:00:54,340 --> 00:01:00,920
so sugar builds up in the blood. High blood sugars over time can cause problems in almost

10
00:01:00,920 --> 00:01:07,680
every part of your body, from your brain to your feet. So treatment is about trying to keep

11
00:01:07,680 --> 00:01:14,900
blood sugars within a target range. Being as active as possible, eating healthy and going

12
00:01:14,900 --> 00:01:21,500
for regular health checks will help you do this. Some people will also need to take insulin or

13
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:27,079
other medication and check their blood sugars regularly. Lots of things can affect blood sugars,

14
00:01:27,560 --> 00:01:33,260
so it can be tricky to balance. But it's possible to lead a full life. It's about being in

15
00:01:33,260 --> 00:01:38,879
tune with your body and learning what works for you. You can get more support from your medical

16
00:01:38,879 --> 00:01:42,000
team and as here at Diabetes UK.

